 "response": "Driril's budget now is **$1528K**.\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office budget changes count. Every message from Sales, PMO, Vendor, Legal and the other teams was ignored.\n2. I worked out each Finance Office withdrawal chain from its last link backwards:\n   - A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect.\n   - The update it targeted is then still in force.\n3. Starting from the $1630K set in #0001, I applied every update that still stands, in record order.\n\n**Examples of withdrawal chains**\n- #0004 (+$237K) stands. #0019 withdrew it, but #0114 withdrew #0019.\n- #0014 (\u2212$222K) is withdrawn. #0035 withdrew it; #0286 withdrew #0035, but #0532 then withdrew #0286, so #0035 holds.\n- #0214 (\u2212$571K) stands. #0225 withdrew it; #0254 withdrew #0225, #1006 withdrew #0254, and #1596 withdrew #1006. That leaves #0254 in force, so #0225 is cancelled.\n- #0473 (\u2212$32K) is withdrawn. The chain #0571 \u2190 #0631 \u2190 #0720 \u2190 #0924 \u2190 #1039 resolves with #0571 in force.\n\n**Running totals at a few points**\n- After #0098: $683K.\n- After #0461: $2194K.\n- After #0804: $3251K.\n- After #1138: $2063K.\n- After #1600: $1528K.\n\nThis is a long hand calculation over about 1,600 records, so a small slip is possible.\n\nANSWER: $1528K",
